  "note": "Both arms are bake-rs at 6852a31140; the on arm sets `subagents: true` through EVAL_SETTINGS_ON. Without the setting the agent has no subagent tool, so every off sample fails the delegation predicate, which requires a subagent call; that failure count and the token and request differences are the point of the comparison, not regressions. Each on sample delegated once and wrote the expected summary. A child's requests pass the proxy but not the parent's event stream, so on samples have usageComplete false and their token figures cover the parent only. One gemini-3.8-flash-high off sample looped for 39 requests rereading the notes without a subagent tool, as it did against develop. The default model surface is unchanged from develop: the first-request fixtures are identical, so the standard suite needs no new pair. steps/1-on-by-default measures the tools on by default against develop on the standard suite: total tokens rose 12 to 19% on every model, with no change in requests or failures, from about 1.7 KB of tool definitions in every request; that cost made them opt-in.",
